Z||000000||ig88vsbobafett||10-30-2001||08:47 PM||||So far i know i need<BR>V6 Moter strut (Dogbone)<BR>V6 Moter mounts <BR>Wiring harness<BR>V6 Moter (2.8/3.1)<P>Is there any Drilling ?? for the new moter mounts<P>I have a 1984 am4 4 speed now (man)<P>Am i missing anything and how much work is it <BR>i have changed a few 350 chevy moters in chevy trucks ||||reg||1
Z||000001||wantav8||10-30-2001||09:28 PM||||the front mounts for the V6 need drilled into the cradle. I have mentioned this before but, let me tell you. Instead of switching complete wiring harness over, just put a carb and regular distributor on it. it will perform almost identical to the Fuel injected.||||reg||1
Z||000002||isthiswhereiputausername?||10-30-2001||09:50 PM||||I switched mine to a 2.8L carbed a few years back.. pretty easy..<P>all mounts will pretty much fit up except for front motor mount (need a v6 one or weld your old one up) and the dogbone (you can also weld a bracket up.. if you have acess to a welder)<P>Carbed was VERY easy, doing only a few wires makes it a lot easier..<P>you will need to modify your exhaust to fit the new manifold..  need any photos or anything, feel free to pm me. <P>||||reg||1
